{
  "title": "Dua of Mother for her child who is ailing.",
  "data": "اَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّنَاۤ اَنْتَ وَهَبْتَهٗ لِيْ وَ لَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا مَّذْكُوْرًا\nALLAAHUMMA RABBANAA ANTA WAHABTAHU LEE WA LAM YAKU SHAY'AM MADHKOORAA\nO Allah, our Lord, You bestowed him upon me when he was nothing mentioned.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاشْفِهٖ بِشِفَآئِكَ وَ دَاوِهٖ بِدَوَآئِكَ وَ عَافِهٖ مِنْ بَلَآئِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FASH-FIHI BI-SHIFAAA'IKA WA DAAWIHI BI-DAWAAA'IKA WA A'AFIHI MIM BALAAA'IK\nO Allah, heal him with Your cure, treat him with Your medicine, and grant him well-being from Your affliction,\nوَ اجْعَلْهُ بَارًّا تَقِيًّا صَالِحًا بِمَنِّكَ وَ كَرَمِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWAJ-A'LHU BAARRAN TAQIYYAN SAALIHAM BI-MANNIKA WA KARAMIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand make him dutiful, pious, and righteous, by Your grace and generosity, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy!",
  "merits": "Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) instructed: If a child is ailing, let the mother ascend to the roof of the house, uncover her head, and fall prostrate before Allah, reciting this supplication:"
}
